# Local video transcript fetcher

## Role
When this rule is applied to a local video, or to a folder of videos, write one transcript per video as a `.txt` file in the **same folder** as that video. Do not download video. Do not call YouTube, Tactiq, or any caption site. Do not commit or push unless the user asks.

Applies to `Personal/course_videos/` and to any other local video or folder the user attaches.

## Task
Save `<video stem>.txt` beside the source. Keep spaces and punctuation in the stem. Recurse into subfolders. Ignore `OLD_FILES`.

Skip a video whose sibling `.txt` already has timestamp cues and reaches the end of the video. If the `.txt` is empty, says `Transcript not available`, or stops well before the end, continue from the last good cue. Do not discard finished cues.

Skip a file named `MERGED*` when that folder also has the source clips. If the folder contains only one video, transcribe it even when the title says "entire" or "merged".

## Tool
From the `Personal` root:

```bash
python bin/transcribe_local_videos.py --file "course_videos/<folder>/<video>.webm"
python bin/transcribe_local_videos.py --dir "course_videos/<folder>"
```

Absolute paths are fine. The script uses `ffmpeg` / `ffprobe` and `faster-whisper`. Install `faster-whisper` only if the import fails (`python -m pip install faster-whisper`). Prefer CUDA `float16`. If inference reports a missing `cublas64_12.dll`, install `nvidia-cublas-cu12` and `nvidia-cudnn-cu12` and add their `bin` folders with `os.add_dll_directory` before loading the model. If CUDA still fails, retry once with `small.en` on CPU and record that fallback in the summary. Do not invent a second pipeline.

Model order: `distil-large-v3`, then `small.en` if the larger model does not fit in GPU memory.

## Process
Work shortest file first when the batch is large.

For each source video:

1. Probe subtitle streams with `ffprobe`. If a text subtitle stream exists (`subrip`, `ass`, `ssa`, `mov_text`, `webvtt`), extract it with `ffmpeg` and turn cues into the timestamp lines below. Do not download a caption.
2. If there is no text subtitle stream, decode mono 16 kHz audio with `ffmpeg` and transcribe it in 10-minute windows with faster-whisper (`language=en`, `vad_filter=True`, `beam_size=1`, `condition_on_previous_text=False`). Do not open the video through PyAV. Add each window's start time to the segment time. `BatchedInferencePipeline` is allowed when it uses those same settings.
3. Write `<stem>.txt` in the video's folder. On a bad or unreadable file, write the placeholder below and continue.

Report progress every 5 videos. On a long file, report every window.

## Output

```
# [Video title from the filename]

Source: [path relative to Personal, forward slashes]
Fetched On: [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS]
Language: English
Transcript Type: Embedded subtitles | Local whisper (distil-large-v3, cuda)

---

[00:00] First segment.
[00:14] Next segment.
```

Use `[MM:SS]` under one hour and `[HH:MM:SS]` at one hour or more. Keep the words the track or the model returned. Do not summarize them in this file.

### Placeholder

```
# [Video title]

Source: [relative path]
Fetched On: [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS]
Language: English
Transcript Type: Unavailable

---

Transcript not available for: [Video title]
Reason: [what failed]
```

### Summary
Write `transcript_summary.md` in each folder you were asked to transcribe: considered, transcribed, skipped, failed (with the reason), and each `.txt` with its source path.

If faster-whisper cannot be imported and cannot be installed, stop. Write that reason once in `course_videos/local_transcript_summary.md`. Do not emit a placeholder per video for a missing tool.

## Quality checklist
- [ ] A finished sibling `.txt` was not regenerated
- [ ] Empty or truncated transcripts were continued, not left incomplete
- [ ] `MERGED*` was skipped only when source clips exist in that folder
- [ ] The `.txt` sits beside the video and uses the video stem
- [ ] Timestamps are present and the source path is in the header
- [ ] `transcript_summary.md` matches the files on disk
- [ ] A failed file records the reason and the batch continues
